[I]Visualize Metadata[/I] is a small plugin to visualize into a chart the metadata statistics in your Calibre library.

The plugin has the following features:
[LIST]
[*]Display the values into different chart[LIST]
[*]Pie
[*]Pie (outline)
[*]Bar
[*]Bar (with gap)
[/LIST]

[*]Limit analyze to scope:[LIST]
[*]Entire library
[*]Virtual library
[*]Current search
[/LIST]

[*]Show top X values[LIST]
[*]or all of them (special value 0)
[/LIST]
[*]Include books without value in the chart

[*]Sorting by:[LIST]
[*]Alphabetical (ascending & descending)
[*]Size (ascending & descending)
[/LIST]

[*]Additional grouping option for date:[LIST]
[*]Year
[*]Month
[*]Day
[*]Hour
[*]Minute
[/LIST]

[*]Export data to CSV or JSON
[/LIST]

This plugin attempt to be a autnomous version and replacement of the similar feature in [URL=https://www.mobileread.com/forums/showthread.php?t=269911]Job Spy[/URL] plugin by DaltonST.

[B]Special Notes:[/B]
[LIST]
[*]If you switch libraries, all dialogs open will be automaticly closed.
[/LIST]

[B]Installation[/B]
Open [I]Preferences -> Plugins -> Get new plugins[/I] and install the "Visualize Metadata" plugin.
You may also download the attached zip file and install the plugin manually, then restart calibre as described in the [URL="https://www.mobileread.com/forums/showthread.php?t=118680"]Introduction to plugins thread[/URL]

The plugin works for Calibre 5 and later.

Page: [URL=https://github.com/un-pogaz/Visualize-Metadata]GitHub[/URL] | [URL=https://www.mobileread.com/forums/showthread.php?t=376313]MobileRead[/URL]

[U]Note for those who wish to provide a translation:[/U]
I am [I]French[/I]! Although for obvious reasons, the default language of the plugin is English, keep in mind that already a translation.
